WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.667
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Today, we are talking

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:04.920
about finding the right tools,
frequently asked questions,

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.060
and editing in the Cloud.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.050
I'm Priyanka, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.230
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.030
Choosing the right
tool for the job

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.760
is essential for getting
something done right.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.470
And Cloud technologies
are no different.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.420
The right tool depends on
highly individualized criteria,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.820
like language
support, compatibility

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.490
with existing tools,
portability, and openness,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.580
and cost.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.420
While you might not know
every product mapping

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.930
across providers, you probably
have the foundational knowledge

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.540
to understand which
product categories are

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.340
the most relevant to you.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.490
That's why we just published
a handy product map

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:48.300
showcasing similar offerings
between Google Cloud, AWS,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.320
and Azure.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.040
Take a look and find out
which tools work best for you.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.130
With all those tools, there
maybe some technologies

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.930
you're not familiar with yet.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:02.040
Thankfully, our editorial team
has put together this quick 101

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.730
guide on some frequently asked
questions and definitions that

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.260
can help you get started, or
brush up on some concepts.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.230
We've just made Doc
AI generally available

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.140
to help you automate
and validate documents

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.690
to streamline your
document workflows.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.420
Whether you're sitting on
a ton of unstructured data

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.060
or looking to reduce
your manual workload,

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.790
Doc AI is the
right tool to help.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.550
What better way to get
started than this guide

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.130
and video from
developer advocate Anu

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.380
to show you how it works?

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.930
Cloud Shell Editor
makes it easy for you

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:41.020
to deploy code to the Cloud
directly from your web browser.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.080
In this video,
developer advocate

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.040
Ryan will show you some of the
features of Cloud Shell Editor,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.410
including integrating
Cloud code,

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:52.350
simplifying Kubernetes
and Cloud-run development

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.610
workflows.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.980
Check it out and stay
tuned for more videos

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.750
around how to use it.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.480
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.200
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.460
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment, or tweet us.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.110
We will see you in the Cloud.

